Finally! My first ascension after 6 months of more or less regular
playing (and about three years after playing the first time). This
ascension wouldn't be possible without the nice RNG which helped me to
find a bunch of good equipment quite soon :) And I was several times
_really_ lucky no to die YAAD!

The game started quite promising since I found a =oSD at about Dlvl 2 or 3
which I happily wear the rest of the game. I didn't died because a lack of
food for a while now but slow disgusting is nevertheless a nice thing.

On Dlvl 3 was a general shop which I visited soon again to sell a diamond
I found (and identified thanks to my touchstone) at the first mine level.
My Pet stole it back and I decided to try to get to the mine-town with my
current experience level (XL 4) to buy cheap protection. This worked
pretty well and after selling my diamond in the general shop in the
mine-town again I was able to get a naked AC of 3. Mine-town was really
great since its shops sold me two magic markers, a magic whistle and a
magic lamp. I used this magic lamp as light source for the rest of the
game although I blessed it later on just in case I need an emergency wish.

Since I died far to often in the lower levels of the mines I headed back
to the main dungeon to do sokoban and look out for an altar. No altar!
Sokoban had the amulet. Back in the mines I found a bag of holding one
level beneath the town. At this point I had two dogs and one cat to
support me in my quest and we cleaned out the mines. Usually I think that
more than one pet is annoying but with a magic whistle it's ok.
Unfortunately I found not a single polymorph trap in the mines so I wasn't
able to "upgrade" my pets. On the other side I was happy not to step in
one myself :)

With my brand new +7 rustproof dwarwish mattock (thanks to some paper
golems and the mentioned magic markers) I felt pretty unstoppable and a
throne on Dlvl 10 which let me wish for a GDSM increased this feeling even
more. Usually a perfect time for YASD! And it nearly happened! A trapdoor
later I found myself alone in the middle of the big room surrounded by a
of monsters with a really bad mood. I panicked an decided to try to run to
the next stairs killing everything which is in my way. After about 10
turns I was completely surrounded. No wand of digging! (and using my
mattock would have taken to long, or not?) Can't remember if I thought
about teleporting or if I just didn't had a possibility to do it. So I
used my wand of lightning to engrave Elbereth. Of course I made a mistake
while engraving and of course I was blinded by the flash! I thought at
this point the game is over since engraving again while bind has only a
small chance of success. (Probably this isn't true; I will try that in one
of my next games.) The next step was to #pray to get to my max 71 HP
again. At this point I was about 4 or 5 squares away from one of the walls
and decided to fight my way in this direction so monsters can "only"
attack me from 5 sides at the same time. When I reached my goal I was down
to about 25 HP again. I slayed on of two hill giants standing in front of
me and suddenly noticed that no monster is attacking me from the left. I
tried to move to the left and hit a boulder I couldn't move since some
beast was behind it. Same for the right side. (Note that I was still blind
at this point) I realized that this boulders were thrown by the hill
giants an instead of killing me they were now protecting me. The same
thing also for the upper-left and upper-right! There was just on giant
left which was standing right in front of me. Killed him and smiled. Down
to about 10 HP but completely surrounded by boulders! So I had time to wait
for a while to heal myself up. Then destroyed one of the boulders and
swung my mattock in the face of every creature that was stupid enough to
look what's behind this boulders. Note for the future: take this two
scrolls of earth from sokoban with you!

After this exciting fight nothing special happened the next 10 Levels.
Except collecting the usual amount of rings, potions, wands, etc. I
was looking hard for an altar but found only one temple at about Dlvl 20
with wasn't co-aligned. I had a lot of money from cleaning out vaults (the
detect treasure spell is really handy for an Archeologist) and donated for
another 2 points of protection. I really needed an altar (especially to
bless my bag of holding and some identify scrolls) but was to afraid to
attack the priest in this temple. (Look at the very end of this post to
see the second place on my high score list if you want to know why) Instead
I went back to mine-town to kill the priest there. I had no stethoscope at
this point but I thought this one might be weaker. Succeeded in doing
that, converted the altar, blessed and identified my equipment.

Then I bought candles the first time ever! Unfortunately only 5 which was
obviously a problem later on in the game.

Medusa was on Dlvl 23. No Titan. Killed the eels with some wands, put on
my ring of levitation and a blindfold (additional to reflection, just to
be sure) and turned her into stone. Everything looked quite good at this
moment. Then I arrived in Dlvl 25 which was the last level before the
castle. I had two pets at this time (a large dog and something else) and
used my magic whistle and a polymorph trap to get an iron golem and a
green dragon. The iron golem survived only about 20 turns ("may he rust in
peace"). The dragon which I named Poisy died a spectacular death later
on in the Valley of Death ... "The black dragon breathes a
disintegration blast!  The blast of disintegration whizzes by you!
Poisy is disintegrated!"

On this level I also found the first co-aligned altar and started to
scarify some monsters to get a nice weapon. After two or three scrolls of
create monster I put on my blindfold and saw a purple "h" coming in my
direction. Great! Another dwarf lord to be sacrified. (STUPID me!) Took
of the blindfold and waited a few turns. Until I got this nice message:
"The invisible master-mind flayer ..." Panic! And why don't I wear my
greased helmet? Put on the helmet on the next turn. Grease was worn of
after the first attack! Suck ... eat ... feeling stupid ... you probably
know that. Time to use the big guns! (I found a wand of death 0:5 in a
chest on my first quest level.) "The death ray misses the invisible
master-mind flayer." Suck ... "The death ray misses ..." Suck ... "The
death ray misses ..." Suck ... "The death ray hits!" Finally! Using my
unicorn horn I was able to get my intelligence from 6 back to 18 again
but of course I forgot almost everything about identified equipment (and
explored levels).

So my next goal was to pray for additional holy water to bless identify
scrolls and to identify everything again. Went to the next fountain to
dip some potions. Some elfs interrupted me and suddenly my bag of
holding was cursed! No idea who did that and how it happened. Being
overtaxed I managed to fall down the nearby stairs and escaped. The first
thing that came into my mind was to #pray and hope that Camaxtli
recognizes the reason for it. Instead I was crowned and got Vorpal Blade.
This is the first time I got crowned but I wasn't that happy about it. A
more clever thing at this moment would have probably been to drop the bag,
go upstairs, dip for a potion of water, pray for holy water, go back and
uncurse it. But of course I couldn't pray now for a while. Since it was
4 am and I was tired I just took a scroll of remove curse out of the
bag. I didn't even look which items disappeared :)

After this stupid mistakes I started to attack the castle. It was the
third time I saw it and I used my old tactic to stay away from the
drawbridge and just destroy it with a wand of striking (already had a
=oL). Sitting on the throne gave me the possibility to wipe out this
annoying master mind flayers. From the castle wand I got: helm of
brilliance, speed boots, 2 scrolls of genocide (wiped out L and kept one
for emergencies) and gauntlets of dexterity.  With this new equipment and
my new XP level 14 I headed back to the quest. On the way Poisy killed
the priest in the temple on level 20.

The quest was no problem at all (had AC below -30). I trained my dagger,
long sword and two-weapon skills. After the quest I suddenly noticed that
I lost all my protection and that my god is displeased. Looks like I
killed to much of this peaceful garter snakes. And the two priests I meet
so far are both dead. So I had to spend 36000 Zorkmids in the valley of
death to get back to a naked AC of 4.  Entered Gehennom to collect
additional 18000 $.

The first demon in my way was Asmodeus who requested about 8500 $ for safe
passage ... not with me! First attack: "Vorpal Blade beheads Asmodeus!
You kill Asmodeus!" The next on was Jubilex and than Baalzebub. No
problems at all. Went back to the valley of death to donated another 12000
$ to the priest of Moloch before my new pet, an angel killed him. He got
the really stupid name "Erzengel Gabriel" after that. Since this angle was
a nice pet I tried to give him some good equipment to prevent that some
black dragon will kill him too. "Erzengel Gabriel removes a banded mail
and puts on a +0 silver dragon scale mail. Status of Erzengel Gabriel
(lawful):  Level 21 HP 168(168)  AC -22, tame, fast." (I lost him later on
somewhere in Gehennom. No idea what was able to kill him.)

The entrance to Vlad's tower was on Dlvl -35. Nothing special to write
about him and his death. After that I moved out of Gehennom to my stash. I
still had only 5 candles. So I collected a huge amount of keys,
blindfolds, lock picks, etc. to polymorph them into candles! I even went
back to the mines to get more "("s. I had the polymorph spell but this
took really a long with the spell at 44% and maximum Pw. 92.
The nice side effect of this procedure: doing a lot of alchemy and hoping
for wands of wishing or death. Looks like you can't get one of those two
wands via ploymorphing. Or I had bad luck.

Than I was finally ready for the endgame! Marked the VS and looked for
Rodney. On one of the entrance levels to his tower I made the last mistake
that nearly killed me. I was shooting with a wand of magic missile on some
krakens or eels. But didn't read the message "Nothing happens" when trying
to zap with the empty wand and instead of zapping in the direction I made
a step towards the water. Luckily I had a wand of teleportation in my main
inventory to teleport the eel away. Wow ... after more than 70000 turns
only one turn away from death. I immediately genocided ";" after that.

The rest of the game wasn't that hard any more. I had 4 wands of death and
some blessed scrolls of charging and whenever Rodney showed (10 times) up
I demonstrated him the effects of the wands.

Well done, mortal!  But now thou must face the final Test...--More--
Prove thyself worthy or perish!--More--

First time the planes! I was quite nervous but I had all the necessary
equipment (?oGD, !oFH, =oC) and I never got into serious trouble.
Astral: first altar on the right was lawful. I meet Famine on the way in
and again on the way out. Two times death ray. Altar in the middle was
guarded by Pestilence. But it was also of wrong alignment. On the way out
I was zapped quite a lot times with all kind of wands and spells. Two of
my wands of death broke and I lost also my old =oSD. Next time I will wear
the amulet of reflection instead of live saving.
On the way to the left I just ignored Death and went right to the altar.


